        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first to get rid of all your cards. You cannot exit if you hold the Joker.',
          gameplay: "1. **Discarding Pairs**: At the start, all players discard any identical pairs from their hand (e.g., two 8s).\n2. **Drawing**: Starting with the dealer's left, a player draws one card FROM the hand of the player to their right.\n3. If they form a pair with the drawn card, they discard it. If not, they keep it.\n4. **The Joker**: If you draw the Joker, you must keep it until an opponent draws it from YOU.",
          keyRules: [
            'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Joker (Exit Game).',
            'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Scoring follows the game-specific point or pot rules.',
            'Winning condition: Be the first to get rid of all your cards.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep the Joker on the 'outside' of your hand fan to make it easier for the person to your left to pick it. Don't act too happy if you get rid of it!",
          intermediate: "Manipulation: Shuffle your hand every time someone is about to draw from you, but try to 'present' a specific card that isn't the Joker to trick them into taking the Joker instead.",
          advanced: "Reverse Psychology: Most players pick cards from the middle of a hand. If you have 3 cards including the Joker, place the Joker in the traditional 'safe' spot (far left/right) and watch your opponent over-think themselves into taking it.",
          tips: [
            'This is a game of luck and poker-faces. Keep your reactions neutral.',
            'The faster the game moves, the easier it is to pass the Joker unnoticed.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
